DDL: CREATE, ALTER, & DROP
Instructions:
Open this repository in the browser as shown in class
Launch the repository via the GitHub Codespace as shown in class and open it with VS Code
When satisfied that you have completed the required changes in the repository folder, commit and push the entire repository as shown in class.
You must ensure that your solution has been pushed to GitHub in order to get credit for the exercise.
Tasks:
Create a DDL script to create the tables shown in the ERD in the image below. Make sure to save this script in a SQL file within the repository.

Your completed script should:

a. Successfully create all five table objects with no errors.

b. Include all columns for each table

c. Include the appropriate datatypes as indicated in the ERD. Please Note: ERD datatypes do not always match the physical datatypes in a particular DB platform, so you may need to do some “translations”.

d. Make use of at least one ALTER command after initially creating the table.

e. Have a DROP section to drop all the tables at the top of the script so that the entire script can be run multiple times to recreate the database structure.

f. Have excellent SQL commenting for each section of the script.

Take a screenshot of the resulting database tables to show that you can successfully run your DDL script and paste it into an image file within the repository called successful_table_creation.bmp.
